WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.230
- We're coming up on award season.

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:03.240
So do you have a favorite
red carpet moment?

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:04.350
You've done a lot of red carpets, right?

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:06.180
So any one that sticks out?

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:08.010
- Well, my favorite award show every year

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:09.120
is the Golden Globes

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:10.200
because it's the first one

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.150
of the year and no one's lost yet.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:13.080
Right?

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:14.169
- Everyone's in good spirits.

00:00:14.169 --> 00:00:15.210
- Everyone's in a good mood.

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:16.710
You get to see everyone, all the

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:18.450
big TV stars and the movie stars.

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:21.120
But you don't know necessarily
who's gonna win because

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.920
by the time the Oscar
comes out, everyone kind of

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:26.310
has an idea of who's going
to win best actor, right?

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:27.750
But everybody's in a
good mood right there.

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.490
And I used to have a
tradition that everybody

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:30.323
was ready to party too.

00:00:30.323 --> 00:00:31.710
'Cause it was the first
one kicking off the year

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:33.270
that I'd bring tequila on the red carpet

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:36.180
and I'd be doing shots with
whoever wanted to do one.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:39.426
Well, listen, I can hold my
tequila, but after a while.

00:00:39.426 --> 00:00:40.950
- I've never had someone do
that for me on a red carpet.

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:42.930
I might do red carpets
if that were happening.

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:44.430
- I remember one time Kelly, it was,

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:46.320
I was like in double digits
and I was still holding it

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:48.750
but then I was talking Reese
Witherspoon, and I was like,

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:50.070
I was maybe a little too close to this.

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:51.120
And she was getting
the biggest kick outta,

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:51.960
I said, I saw myself.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:53.823
I said, oh my God, no more tequila.

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:55.680
- Double digits?

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:57.720
You're the real man.

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:58.553
- Yeah, oh yeah.

00:00:58.553 --> 00:00:59.386
- I can't do that.

00:00:59.386 --> 00:01:00.219
- I'm a real Mexican.

00:01:00.219 --> 00:01:03.213
- I was like, I'm texting,
I like tequila too, but I,

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:07.140
I would be on the floor
with double digits.

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:10.350
It would be a different, I'd
be interviewing like this.

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:11.580
They would never allow me to do that.

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:12.413
- It was fun.

00:01:12.413 --> 00:01:13.246
But now as you get older, you know,

00:01:13.246 --> 00:01:14.640
I gotta, I gotta keep it
in check a little bit.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:15.630
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:16.740
It does sound fun though.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:17.573
- [Mario] Yeah. It's a good time.

00:01:17.573 --> 00:01:19.740
- 'Cause sometimes, you know,
people get the same questions,

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:21.270
you know, we often have
to ask the same thing.

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:22.170
So it's like,

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.450
it's nice when something
breaks it up like that.

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:25.283
That's fun.

00:01:25.283 --> 00:01:26.116
- Yeah. So that's, that's
probably my favorite

00:01:26.116 --> 00:01:26.949
to answer your question.

00:01:26.949 --> 00:01:27.851
- [Kelly] Oh my God.

